course: dictionary
lesson: 13180
title: Informal words and fair play
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to everyday talk rather than formal writing. Freeload is one of them. It means to take food, money, a place to stay or other things from others without paying or helping back.
explain: «He's always freeloading at our house.» The clues are that he is at the house all the time and never pays or helps. Freeload is a criticism, so the speaker thinks it is unfair.
explain: A person who does this is called a freeloader. Try your meaning in the sentence: "He's always taking food and a place to stay without paying or helping at our house" still makes sense, so you have worked it out.
fact: «Freeload» is an informal verb, used in everyday talk.
fact: «Freeload» means to take food, money, a place to stay or other things without paying or helping.
fact: A «freeloader» is a person who freeloads.
fact: It is disapproving: it tells you the person is being unfair or lazy.
fact: The other forms are freeloads, freeloaded and freeloading.
exercise: «Tom never buys his own snacks; he just freeloads off his friends.» What does freeloads mean? | Plays games with his friends every day | Gives his friends money to help them | *Takes things from others without paying or helping | Chooses the best snacks in the shop
exercise: Which word means a person who freeloads? | leader | teacher | freezer | *freeloader
exercise: «The lodger freeloaded on his cousin for a whole year and never paid any rent.» Does the author think this is fair? | Yes, it is kind and generous | No, because a year is too short | *No, it is unfair, because he took a place to stay without paying or helping | Yes, because the cousin wanted him there
test: «Ella's brother freeloads on her pocket money every week.» What does freeloads mean here? | Saves his own money carefully | Gives her presents | *Takes her money without paying her back or helping | Earns money by helping at home
test: Which sentence uses freeload correctly? | Mum freeloads the washing up every night. | The freeloader bakes a cake for everyone. | Freeloading is a sport played in the park. | *Sam freeloads his sister's sweets and never buys any of his own.
exam: What does «freeload» mean? | To share a meal fairly with friends | *To take things from others without paying or helping | To pay for everything you use | To lend money to a family member
